===== E321
| Page 238 | 5782 | mssEC 25 (obj 5952, pointer 5782), 1 Sept 1864 Head Qrs A. P., Caldwell to Eckert: cable to be laid on the north side of the river, less danger from anchors, channel nearest the south shore (FM-R7b; FIX-FM12, AUDIT FV-FM10b s.5; row 5782/0; image-read at 2400 px; two cipher copies: 5781 foot in wire order, 12319 received copy)
Maj. Eckert Di - Sheldon F
I think cab bell should be laid
on tremble side of windsor as it
will take less cab bell and will
be less danger of being dragged up
by anchors and channel most of way
is nearest waxy shore D do wren
Caldwell
